          "correctOptionId": "4",
          "marks": 1,
          "negativeMarks": 0.25,
          "explanation": "<p><strong>Given</strong>: An uncertain number of persons are sitting in a row facing the north.</p>\n\n<p>Based on the given conditions, we get-</p>\n\n<p>1.&nbsp; F sits at the extreme right end of the row. Only one person sits between F and B. X sits fifth from the right end of the row. G sits second to the left of X. From these, we get-</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"//storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/24/06/F1_Banking_Savita_25-06-24_D10.png\" style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); height: 66px; width: 159px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>2. N sits fourth to the left of X. Only two persons sit between N and T. Only one person sits between N and G. From these, we get-</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"//storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/24/06/F1_Banking_Savita_25-06-24_D11.png\" style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); height: 66px; width: 271px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>3. Only four persons sit to the left of U. T sits third to the right of U. R sits to the immediate left of T. A sits second to the right of T. From these, we get the final arrangement as follows-</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"//storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/24/06/F1_Banking_Savita_25-06-24_D12.png\" style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); height: 66px; width: 430px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>From the final arrangement, we see that a total of nineteen persons sit in the row.</p>\nHence, <strong>19 persons sit in the linear row facing north</strong>.",
